{"additions":23,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"The taglines and concept text still described the original diff viewer. vig now watches git, GitHub issues / PRs / CI runs / project boards, containers, processes and worktrees — the things you keep an eye on while work (human or agent) happens in a repository.\n\nUpdated: README (en/ja) tagline, `Cargo.toml` description (lands on crates.io with the next release), the Homebrew formula `desc`, the CLAUDE.md Concept section, and both guide intros. The name and the repo-rooted model are unchanged (vig = vim + git). The GitHub repository description and topics were updated directly alongside this PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":7,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T08:36:43Z","deletions":16,"headRefName":"docs/repositioning","labels":[],"number":142,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLd8m8A","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe changes are limited to documentation and release metadata copy updates and appear consistent and low-risk.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR updates vig’s public-facing positioning from a side-by-side diff viewer to a read-only TUI “cockpit” for monitoring busy repositories and surrounding tooling (git + GitHub + local system context), aligning documentation and release metadata with the current product scope.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Refreshes the main README and Japanese README tagline/intro to describe vig as a read-only TUI cockpit.\n- Updates both English/Japanese user guide introductions to match the new concept framing.\n- Updates release-facing metadata strings (Cargo crate description and Homebrew formula `desc`) and the repo’s internal concept doc (`CLAUDE.md`).\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| README.md | Updates the top-level tagline to the new “read-only TUI cockpit” positioning. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Updates the Japanese tagline to match the new positioning. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/introduction.md | Reframes the English guide introduction around the cockpit concept and enumerates monitored surfaces. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/introduction.md | Reframes the Japanese guide introduction around the cockpit concept and enumerates monitored surfaces. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates the Concept section to reflect the cockpit framing and reinforces non-mutating constraints. |\r\n| Cargo.toml | Updates the crates.io description string to match the new positioning. |\r\n| .github/workflows/release.yml | Updates the generated Homebrew formula `desc` string to match the new positioning. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 7/7 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T08:38:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"84615c979ab7b23e75641a116057ad27db37b7cd"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:49:16Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33374693551/job/99433465392","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-0